  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nTuesday night through Friday night\nAssessment...high (>80%) confidence of near normal temperatures\n\nLow level flow will become more southerly during the week which will \nslowly raise humidity levels.\n\nA weak system is progged to move through the area late Tuesday night \ninto Wednesday but the moisture is lacking. The trend with rain \nchances has been a slow decrease and I would not be surprised to see \nan additional 5-10% decrease from the current 20-30% chance. The \nrelatively 'better' forcing is north of I-80 which is closer to the \nlow track.\n\nSaturday through Monday\nAssessment...low (20-30%) chances for any rain\n\nBy the weekend de-amplification of the flow pattern aloft will occur \nacross the CONUS. During this change a flat ridge will be centered \nfrom the southern Plains into the upper Midwest. Thus while more \nsystems will potentially be moving through the area, they will be \ntopping the ridge axis and would thus be at their weakest.\n\nAny Gulf moisture for the systems has to come up through west Texas \nbefore turning northeast into the Plains.\n\nRight now the model consensus has mainly 15-30% chances for rain \nSaturday through Monday with the better rain chances north of I-80. \nIn looking at the AIGFS and AIFS, rain chances are not as good which \nwould support a further reduction in rain chances as the week \nprogresses.",
